# Local development — per-user overrides that must never be committed.
#
# `.local/` and `*.local` alone did NOT cover the two files this section exists
# for: gitignore patterns match the WHOLE basename, and `settings.local.json` /
# `CLAUDE.local.md` end in `.json` / `.md`, not `.local`. They were ignored on
# the maintainer's machine only by a personal ~/.config/git/ignore, so a cloner
# got no protection at all. The real filenames are listed explicitly below.
# (Comments get their own line: gitignore has no trailing-comment syntax — a `#`
# after a pattern is part of the pattern.)

# a directory a tool parks local state in
.local/
# files whose basename really does end in `.local` (e.g. `.env.local`)
*.local

# Claude Code per-user override files: the Local settings layer and personal
# memory. `**/` so nested workspaces (apps/<name>/.claude/, a product subdir)
# are covered too, not just the repo root.
#
# Local settings layer: personal permissions/env, never shared
**/.claude/settings.local.json
# personal memory, concatenated AFTER CLAUDE.md so it wins without editing core
**/CLAUDE.local.md

# Structured Logging (ignore log files, keep structure)
.logic-loom/logs/operations/*.log
.logic-loom/logs/git-checkpoints/*.json
.logic-loom/logs/parallel-sessions/*
!.logic-loom/logs/README.md

